      grammarTitle: "Past continuous and interruption",
      grammarArabic: "نستخدم was أو were مع ing لوصف فعل جارٍ في وقت ماضٍ، والماضي البسيط للحدث الذي وقع أثناءه.",
      grammarExamples: <String>["Amal was reading when the notice arrived.", "They were waiting while the guide called.", "The sea became rough while they were packing."],
      listening: "Today's island ferry has been canceled because of rough weather. Passengers may move their tickets to tomorrow without a change fee, but tomorrow's sailing is not yet confirmed. Please check the operator's update after six this evening before arranging transport to the terminal. If you no longer wish to travel, speak to the ticket office about the refund conditions. Our staff cannot change hotel bookings, so contact your accommodation provider directly about any delay.",
